      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the context before improving understandability.Now I have a clear picture. The test verifies that `normaliseWhitespace` correctly collapses multiple spaces into one when the input string starts with a Unicode supplementary character (encoded as a surrogate pair). I'll improve understandability by introducing named constants with explanatory comments and structuring the assertions more clearly.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version introduces named constants (`CJK_SUPPLEMENTARY_CHAR`, `HIRAGANA_WITH_COMBINING`) with explanatory comments about the Unicode characters involved, uses descriptive variable names (`inputWithDoubleSpace`, `expectedSingleSpace`), and adds assertion messages that explain the intent — making the test's purpose immediately clear without changing any runtime behaviour."
